#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.desktop.in:3
msgid "Pigoune"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.desktop.in:4
msgid "Organize, find and reuse your icons, logos and illustrations"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.desktop.in:11
msgid "icons;logos;svg;assets;library;graphics;"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.desktop.in:16
msgid "Take a Screenshot"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:8
msgid "Organize, find and reuse your graphic assets"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:10
msgid ""
"All your graphic assets, organized and within reach. Drop your icons, logos "
"and illustrations into Pigoune: it keeps a safe copy, helps you organize "
"them and gives them back with a simple drag and drop."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:16
msgid ""
"Import SVG, PNG, JPEG, WebP, AVIF, HEIC, JPEG XL, GIF, TIFF, BMP, ICO, PSD, "
"Krita, OpenRaster, ICNS, SVGZ, TGA, DDS, QOI, EXR and HDR files"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:17
msgid "Organize with nested collections, smart collections, tags and favorites"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:18
msgid ""
"Find anything instantly with search and filters, also from the GNOME search"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:19
msgid "Reuse assets with drag and drop or the clipboard"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:20
msgid "Convert assets to PNG, JPEG, WebP, AVIF or ICO, at any size"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:21
msgid "Take screenshots or paste images and annotate them in the app"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:22
msgid "Portable libraries, fully local, original files never touched"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:29
msgid "Browse your graphic assets in a thumbnail grid"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:33
msgid "Narrow down your library with search and filters"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:37
msgid "Look closely at an asset and step through its animation"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:41
msgid "Convert assets to PNG, JPEG, WebP, AVIF or ICO"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:45
msgid "See what your library holds, in light or dark style"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:49
msgid "Combine words with “and” or “or” in one click"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:53
msgid "Save a search as a smart collection that fills itself"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:57
msgid "Find the images that fit your screen"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:61
msgid "Frame any image and set it as your wallpaper"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:65
msgid "Nest your tags and browse them level by level"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:69
msgid "Check that every file of your library is still there and intact"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:73
msgid "Annotate a screenshot or any image without touching the original"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:77
msgid "Layers, hand-drawn looks and panels that fold away"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:114
msgid ""
"Keep more kinds of files in your library, and see Photoshop files more "
"faithfully."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:116
msgid ""
"New formats: Krita (KRA) and OpenRaster (ORA) files, shown from the merged "
"image they hold; macOS icons (ICNS), old ones included; compressed SVG "
"(SVGZ), drawn as a vector; and texture and render files (TGA, DDS, QOI, "
"OpenEXR and Radiance HDR)."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:117
msgid ""
"Photoshop files are read faster and with less memory, even large layered "
"ones. Transparent areas stay transparent, files saved without a merged image "
"are recognized, and the preview says why a file cannot be shown."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:118
msgid ""
"The library format moves to 16. Older versions of Pigoune cannot open a "
"library after this version has opened it, and say so."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:124
msgid ""
"Find your assets from the GNOME search, and keep Photoshop files in your "
"library."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:126
msgid ""
"Type in the GNOME search and Pigoune offers the matching assets with a "
"preview. Click one to see it in the library, or click Pigoune to continue "
"the search there. Turn it on in the Search settings of GNOME."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:127
msgid ""
"PSD files are imported, found and shown from their merged image, and can be "
"copied, exported or used as a wallpaper. Layers are not shown and the file "
"stays untouched."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:128
msgid ""
"In Files, right-click images and choose Open With Pigoune to add them to the "
"library, in Unclassified."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:129
msgid ""
"The library format moves to 15. Older versions of Pigoune cannot open a "
"library after this version has opened it, and say so."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:135
msgid ""
"Add comic speech bubbles to your annotated images, and keep the tools, "
"properties and layers always in view."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:137
msgid ""
"The new Bubble tool draws a comic bubble: an oval, a rounded rectangle or a "
"thought cloud, with a tail you can aim anywhere by dragging its round handle "
"(it stops one bubble size from the edge) and text centered inside."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:138
msgid ""
"Type in a comic font (Comic Neue, included with Pigoune) or in the normal "
"font, in bold or italic. Turn on a soft or a hard shadow, a hand-drawn look, "
"or a dashed outline for a whisper."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:139
msgid ""
"While you turn an arrow, a line or a pen stroke, its frame keeps its shape "
"and the angle is shown next to the handle."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:140
msgid ""
"The tools are a small grid of icons, and Properties and Layers are always "
"shown below, with a handle to share their height. Hover a tool to see its "
"name and shortcut. F9 still hides the panel."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:141
msgid ""
"Older versions of Pigoune keep your bubbles when they open an annotated "
"image, but do not draw them."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:147
msgid ""
"Choose your theme, see which collections are left out of the duplicate "
"search, and get your thumbnails back after clearing them."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:149
msgid ""
"Three round buttons at the top of the main menu, and of the menu of the "
"welcome page, follow the system or always use the light or the dark theme. "
"The choice applies at once and is remembered."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:150
msgid ""
"The Left Out button of the Duplicates tab lists the collections left out of "
"the duplicate search, with where each one sits and how many sub-collections "
"go with it, and Include brings one back. The sidebar no longer shows a mark "
"for them."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:151
msgid ""
"After Clear next to the thumbnails in Manage Library, Pigoune makes them "
"again quietly in the background, while you are not using it."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:157
msgid ""
"Show the original of an annotated image in your file manager, and drag "
"images out of a library opened with the folder chooser."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:159
msgid ""
"Show Original replaces View Original: it opens your file manager on the "
"untouched image stored in the library, instead of starting another "
"application that could fail to launch."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:160
msgid ""
"For an annotated image, Show in Files now shows a copy of the annotated "
"image. An image that is not annotated is shown as before."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:161
msgid ""
"Dragging an image out of Pigoune into the file manager works again for a "
"library opened with the folder chooser. The file manager used to show a "
"forbidden cursor."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:162
msgid "A drag whose files cannot be prepared now says so."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:168
msgid ""
"Turn your annotations, resize a text, and leave collections out of the "
"duplicate search."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:170
msgid ""
"Turn a rectangle, an ellipse, a text, a line, an arrow, a pen stroke, a "
"highlighter, a blur or a pixelation with the round handle above it, by steps "
"of 15 degrees while you hold Shift, or set an exact angle with the Rotation "
"setting of the panel."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:171
msgid ""
"A selected text has handles like the other annotations: drag one to make the "
"letters bigger or smaller."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:172
msgid ""
"The spotlight can leave a rounded rectangle lit, steps are bigger and can "
"grow larger, and a blur can go up to a radius of 150."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:173
msgid ""
"A layer is renamed with a double click on its name, or with a second click "
"once it is selected, and its name can be dragged to reorder the layers."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:174
msgid ""
"A collection can be left out of the duplicate search from its menu in the "
"sidebar, and Undo brings it back."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:175
msgid ""
"A blur now hides everything up to the edges of the image. Before, a blur "
"very close to an edge could let a faint trace of the sharp image show "
"through. Images annotated earlier are drawn again without it."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:176
msgid ""
"Files that Pigoune hands to other applications, for an export, a copy or an "
"opening, each get a folder of their own and are cleaned up after a while, "
"and Pigoune refuses a library or a cache folder that is a link."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:177
msgid ""
"Pigoune is quicker with large libraries. The grid and the counts in the "
"sidebar are no longer rebuilt after every import or background analysis, "
"stored thumbnails appear before the original is checked, and dragging many "
"assets out of Pigoune is smoother."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:178
msgid ""
"A library opened with this version can no longer be opened with Pigoune 3.0 "
"or older."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:184
msgid "Capture your screen and annotate it, right inside Pigoune."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:186
msgid ""
"Take a screenshot with Take a Screenshot (Ctrl+Shift+S, the import menu, the "
"launcher icon, or the pigoune --capture command that your desktop can bind "
"to a shortcut), or paste an image with Paste and Annotate (Ctrl+Shift+V). "
"The image opens in an editor inside the window of your library."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:187
msgid ""
"Annotate with rectangles, ellipses, lines, curved or tapered arrows, a pen, "
"a highlighter, numbered or lettered steps, texts with a bubble or an "
"outline, a spotlight, and a blur or a pixelation to hide what is private. "
"Hold Shift for straight lines and perfect squares, pick colors from the "
"image with the eyedropper, choose each tool with a letter, and let the "
"guides align what you move."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:188
msgid ""
"Draw shapes, lines and arrows with a solid, dashed or dotted stroke, and "
"give them a precise, sketchy or very sketchy hand-drawn look."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:189
msgid ""
"Annotations stay editable: the untouched capture is kept next to the "
"annotated image, which is the one shown and exported. Annotate reopens it "
"and View Original shows the capture as it was."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:190
msgid ""
"Layers let you reorder, hide and lock annotations, and the panels of the "
"editor fold away, or hide altogether with F9, to leave room for the image."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:191
msgid ""
"In the detailed preview, hold a button on an annotated image to see the "
"original for as long as you press it."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:192
msgid ""
"Pigoune warns you before you copy, export or open with another application "
"an image whose blur or pixelation is hidden, and refuses to drag it out."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:193
msgid ""
"Copy or export the annotated image as a PNG, or save it in the library, "
"where it receives the capture tag. A capture being edited is kept as a draft "
"if Pigoune closes."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:194
msgid ""
"A library opened with this version can no longer be opened with Pigoune 2.12 "
"or older."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:200
msgid "When look-alikes are not duplicates, you can now tell Pigoune so."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:202
msgid ""
"Ignore Group, in the “⋯” menu of a group, and Not a Duplicate, in the menu "
"of a row, stop Pigoune from offering those assets together. Ignored (N) "
"lists them, Stop Ignoring brings one back, Show All Again brings them all "
"back, and Undo works for each."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:203
msgid ""
"The Duplicates tab is lighter: the trash button only appears once something "
"is ticked, and each group has a clearer title."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:204
msgid ""
"The fine details used to find duplicates now live in their own file in the "
"cache folder, which keeps the database small. If that file is lost or "
"damaged, Pigoune makes it again."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:205
msgid ""
"A library opened with this version can no longer be opened with Pigoune 2.11 "
"or older."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:211
msgid "Pigoune is fast again after the update to 2.11.0."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:213
msgid ""
"Opening a library and Manage Library are quick again, above all for a "
"library stored where files are read through a sandbox portal."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:214
msgid ""
"The background analysis of your assets starts a moment after a library "
"opens, waits while you are using Pigoune, and stops when you open another "
"library. Manage Library shows how far it has got."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:215
msgid ""
"The fine details used to find duplicates are now computed when you first "
"search for duplicates, for the assets that could be duplicates only, with a "
"progress bar."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:221
msgid ""
"The Duplicates tab is rebuilt so that nothing can go to the trash by "
"accident."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:223
msgid ""
"Nothing is ticked for you any more: choose the asset to keep, then tick, one "
"by one, the assets to move to the trash. A confirmation lists exactly what "
"will move, and Pigoune checks every asset again just before moving it."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:224
msgid ""
"Groups only gather assets that all look alike, each marked Identical or "
"Probable, instead of chaining assets that merely resemble a neighbor. "
"Pigoune now compares colors and details too."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:225
msgid ""
"Pigoune analyzes your assets again in the background to learn these details. "
"A library opened with this version can no longer be opened with Pigoune 2.10 "
"or older."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:226
msgid ""
"Earlier versions could offer unrelated assets as duplicates, and Keep This "
"One could send them all to the trash. They stay in the trash until it is "
"emptied or, if automatic emptying is on, for 30 days: open Trash and restore "
"the ones you want."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:232
msgid ""
"Searching for look-alikes is more accurate, and the Duplicates tab is much "
"faster."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:234
msgid ""
"Find Similar no longer offers assets of a very different shape or color, "
"such as a tall wallpaper for a small logo, and puts the assets with the "
"closest colors first."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:235
msgid ""
"The Duplicates tab shows its list at once, loads thumbnails as you scroll, "
"shows a progress bar while searching, and keeps large groups short with a "
"Show More button."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:241
msgid ""
"Pigoune can now find assets that look alike, even in another format or size."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:243
msgid ""
"Right-click an asset and choose Find Similar to list the assets that "
"resemble it, closest first."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:244
msgid ""
"A new Duplicates tab in Manage Library groups assets that look alike, such "
"as the same logo as a PNG and an SVG. Keep the one you want: the others go "
"to the trash, and Undo brings them back."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:245
msgid ""
"Pigoune analyzes your assets in the background after a library opens. A "
"library opened with this version can no longer be opened with Pigoune 2.9 or "
"older."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:246
msgid ""
"A message no longer loses its text when a name contains an ampersand or an "
"angle bracket."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:252
msgid ""
"Asset names can be turned into plain text, and a click next to a thumbnail "
"no longer selects it."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:254
msgid ""
"A new option in Preferences, under Display, makes asset names plain text. A "
"name that is not clickable counts as empty space: a selection rectangle can "
"start from it, and nothing is selected, opened or dragged from it."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:255
msgid ""
"Clicking just outside a thumbnail no longer selects it: the clickable area "
"is now exactly the thumbnail and its name."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:261
msgid ""
"Undo and Redo get their own buttons, the keyboard shortcuts can be changed, "
"and moving assets is clearer."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:263
msgid ""
"Two buttons at the top of the sidebar undo and redo your changes. The "
"message after an undo offers to redo it, and the message after a redo offers "
"to undo it again."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:264
msgid ""
"The keyboard shortcuts can be changed in Preferences, on the new Shortcuts "
"page. Standard ones such as copy, paste and undo are locked, and actions "
"like exporting or importing a folder can be given a key."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:265
msgid ""
"New shortcuts: Ctrl+K adds the selection to a collection, Ctrl+M moves it, "
"Ctrl+T adds a tag, Ctrl+Shift+Z redoes and Ctrl+W closes the window."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:266
msgid ""
"Dragging assets from All or Unclassified into a collection now moves them, "
"and holding Ctrl adds them without removing them from their other "
"collections. Dropping assets on Unclassified removes them from all their "
"collections."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:267
msgid ""
"Adding, removing, favoriting, tagging and moving assets, collections and "
"tags now show a message with Undo, whether you use a drag, a menu or a key. "
"Refused drops explain why."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:268
msgid ""
"Manage Library opens at once instead of waiting for the disk, which was slow "
"for libraries kept behind the Flatpak document portal."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:274
msgid ""
"Choose from 294 icons for your collections, sorted by theme, and enjoy a "
"faster, steadier Pigoune."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:276
msgid ""
"Collections now offer 294 icons in 13 themes, with a search field to find "
"one quickly. Collections you already customized keep their look."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:277
msgid ""
"Searching, filtering and the sidebar counts are several times faster on "
"large libraries."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:278
msgid ""
"Marking a favorite, adding a tag or renaming an asset no longer rebuilds the "
"grid: your scroll position and selection stay put."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:279
msgid "The records in Manage Library now show their thumbnails at once."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:280
msgid ""
"The collection icons come from Phosphor Icons, credited in the About dialog."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:281
msgid ""
"Libraries stay compatible with older versions, but a collection with one of "
"the new icons shows a gray folder in Pigoune 2.6.1 and earlier."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:287
msgid "A fix for a crash when dragging assets over the tags."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:289
msgid ""
"Pigoune no longer closes when you hold dragged assets over a tag with sub-"
"tags, then move the pointer out of the tag list."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:295
msgid ""
"A finishing release: simpler tag navigation, accurate counts, wider image "
"support and much faster deletion of large selections."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:297
msgid ""
"Clicking a tag now shows it and opens its sub-tags at once, and holding "
"dragged assets over a tag with sub-tags for a second opens that level so you "
"can drop them deeper."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:298
msgid ""
"The numbers beside tags and collections follow the search and the filters, "
"and tags with no match are dimmed."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:299
msgid ""
"HEIC photos can be imported when your system can decode them, and unusual "
"ICO, BMP, AVIF and SVG files are recognized more reliably."
msgstr ""
"HEIC-foto’s kunnen worden geïmporteerd als uw systeem ze kan decoderen, en "
"ongewone ICO-, BMP-, AVIF- en SVG-bestanden worden beter herkend."

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:300
msgid ""
"Deleting a large selection is much faster, and SVG files built to exhaust "
"memory are refused."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:301
msgid ""
"Show in Files and Move to for collections join menus that are now ordered "
"the same way everywhere."
msgstr ""
"‘Tonen in Bestanden’ en ‘Verplaatsen naar…’ voor verzamelingen vullen menu’s "
"aan die nu overal op dezelfde manier geordend zijn."

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:302
msgid ""
"Keyboard and screen reader access to the preview and the tags is better, and "
"a failed export says what went wrong."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:308
msgid ""
"Tags can now be nested, the library can check its own health, and the "
"interface uses one consistent vocabulary."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:310
msgid ""
"Nest tags like Subject › Animals › goat: type a path with a slash, browse "
"the tags level by level in the sidebar, and move, merge or delete a tag "
"together with its sub-tags."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:311
msgid ""
"The new Health tab of Manage Library finds missing, damaged and unrecorded "
"files, and lets you add, replace, remove or trash them."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:312
msgid ""
"Export the whole library as folders, and import images dragged straight from "
"a web browser."
msgstr ""
"Exporteer de hele bibliotheek als mappen en importeer afbeeldingen die je "
"rechtstreeks uit een webbrowser sleept."

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:313
msgid ""
"The search field shows where it searches, and a magnifier opens the search "
"in narrow windows."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:314
msgid ""
"The French interface now says “élément” instead of “ressource”, with the "
"same wording in the other languages, and Manage Library is laid out in a "
"centered column."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:315
msgid ""
"Libraries opened with Pigoune 2.5 can no longer be opened with older "
"versions."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:321
msgid ""
"A short window now tells you what is new after each update, and clearing the "
"thumbnails moves to the library information."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:323
msgid ""
"A short window sums up the main news the first time a new version starts. "
"You can turn it off in the Preferences."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:324
msgid ""
"Clearing the thumbnails is now done in the Storage tab of the library "
"information, next to the space they take, instead of in the Preferences."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:330
msgid ""
"Much faster on large libraries, a clearer wallpaper window and shorter, "
"simpler tags."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:332
msgid ""
"Opening a library and searching are several times faster, and scrolling "
"through thousands of thumbnails stays smooth, even before they have been "
"created."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:333
msgid ""
"A tag is now a single word of up to 20 characters: a space ends the tag you "
"are typing and a hyphen joins several words. Existing tags are left as they "
"are."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:334
msgid ""
"The wallpaper framing window is rearranged around the virtual screen, with a "
"discreet note when the image will look blurry."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:335
msgid ""
"Long names are shortened instead of stretching the panels, and the windows "
"fit the narrowest size even with larger text."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:336
msgid ""
"The search finds œ and æ when you type oe and ae, and exporting can no "
"longer ask for a size that would crash Pigoune."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:337
msgid ""
"Pigoune now tells you when an image cannot be loaded and when links were "
"ignored while importing a folder."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:343
msgid "Turn your images into wallpapers, framed exactly the way you want."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:345
msgid ""
"Frame an image on a virtual copy of your screen, under the bars of your "
"desktop, and set it as your wallpaper."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:346
msgid ""
"Fill the empty space with a color of the image, a gradient, a blur or a "
"mosaic, and darken or mirror the image if you wish."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:347
msgid ""
"Filter assets by shape and keep only the images that fit your screen, also "
"in smart collections."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:348
msgid ""
"Libraries opened with Pigoune 2.2 can no longer be opened with older "
"versions."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:354
msgid "Pigoune speaks more languages and looks the same everywhere."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:356
msgid ""
"The interface is now available in German, Spanish, Brazilian Portuguese, "
"Italian, Dutch and Polish."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:357
msgid ""
"Choose the language of Pigoune in the preferences, or keep the one of your "
"system."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:358
msgid "The icons of Pigoune are the same on every distribution."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:364
msgid ""
"A fresh look for the sidebar, the details and the preview, collections with "
"their own icon and color, and a search by color."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:366
msgid "Each collection can have its own icon and color."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.gor3pig.Pigoune.metainfo.xml.in:367
msgid "Filter assets by their main colors, or by any color you pick."
